WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 3.2 · Structure, Governance & Accountability
Organisational structures and organigrams

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Draw the structure you start with and the one you expect as you grow, and change it on purpose.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.541
An organigram is a simple chart of roles and who reports to whom. It shows how the work is organised, not who approves spending or how decisions are made.

4
00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:26.541
Common shapes to start from

5
00:00:26.541 --> 00:00:39.352
Functional: Roles grouped by expertise, such as delivery, finance and communications. Most new organisations start here. For example: Our bakery: one founder leads baking and training, the other sales, accounts and trainee support.

6
00:00:39.352 --> 00:00:49.941
Programme or product: Roles grouped around each programme, product or service you offer. For example: Two leads at our bakery: one for bread sales, one for the traineeship programme.

7
00:00:49.941 --> 00:01:02.470
Network or hub: A small core of founders coordinating partners and volunteers around them. For example: The two bakery founders coordinate the youth centre, the shared kitchen and their café buyers.

8
00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:03.470
Why draw it now

9
00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.774
1. Everyone can see who does what and who to ask.

10
00:01:08.774 --> 00:01:14.448
2. You notice when one founder becomes the bottleneck for every decision.

11
00:01:14.448 --> 00:01:21.122
3. Funders and partners see a real, honest picture of your team.

12
00:01:21.522 --> 00:01:22.122
What it guides

13
00:01:22.122 --> 00:01:27.796
1. Your governance, shown apart from management, even with the same founders.

14
00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:33.470
2. Your role cards and delegation of authority, built on these lines.

15
00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:40.885
3. Your growth: the chart for today and for two or three years ahead.

16
00:01:41.285 --> 00:01:41.885
What to avoid

17
00:01:41.885 --> 00:01:46.078
Drawing ten empty boxes to look established.

18
00:01:46.078 --> 00:01:51.011
Mixing governance and management in one set of lines.

19
00:01:51.011 --> 00:01:58.056
Using personal details instead of role names, or changing shape by accident.

20
00:01:58.656 --> 00:02:00.456
You map your starting roles, reporting lines and capacity gaps.

21
00:02:00.456 --> 00:02:04.456
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:05.956 --> 00:02:09.056
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
